VortX original local-file witness prerequisite.

Base: 8c67647b50059406c5c0444903597281b81516cf.
Apply after the retained platform patches and HTTP/audio/gpu-next backports.

Freeze regular-file identity and a non-reused source generation at the original
native open. The read-only vortx-original-local-file property returns stored
scalars under the native core, never a late pathname lookup or a descriptor.
Timeline wrappers without an original stream and unsupported sources refuse.
The version-1 map has four identity fields plus a typed osc-disabled flag;
no-Lua targets report true explicitly rather than relying on a missing option.

This is source-provenance evidence, not immutable-content proof, a descriptor
grant, stream-index mapping, subtitle alignment, or a final-mount capability.
Consumers still need original descriptor matching, revalidation, and their
original load/manual-revision/account/profile/epoch admission. Existing public
C headers, commands, version pins, playback behavior and subtitle loading are
unchanged. Generation capture is supported on Apple/Linux; other platforms
remain compilable but have no witness. No paths, URLs or cue bytes are added to
the property or logging.

